Lepton: NV12 buffers that VA-API drivers can decode into

gbm cannot allocate NV12, so gbm_mesa lays it out by hand in a linear R8
allocation: row pitch = width, and the modifier gbm reports for that
allocation (DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID on radeonsi). Decoding straight into
such buffers (Codec2 FFmpeg service, DRM PRIME mode) failed: radeonsi
refused the import of a 160-pixel-pitch surface, and iHD decoded with its
own aligned pitch, so the picture was sheared.

Give spoofed NV12 256-byte row pitches and report it as linear.

diff --git a/gbm_mesa_driver/gbm_mesa_internals.cpp b/gbm_mesa_driver/gbm_mesa_internals.cpp
--- a/gbm_mesa_driver/gbm_mesa_internals.cpp
+++ b/gbm_mesa_driver/gbm_mesa_internals.cpp
@@ -401,8 +401,14 @@
 	};
 
 	if (alloc_args.drm_format == 0) {
-		/* Always use linear for spoofed format allocations. */
-		drv_bo_from_format(bo, alloc_args.width, 1, alloc_args.height, format);
+		/* Always use linear for spoofed format allocations. Lepton: NV12
+		 * (video decoder output) gets 256-byte row pitches, which VA-API
+		 * drivers need to decode into the buffer (radeonsi refuses others,
+		 * iHD writes with its own aligned pitch). */
+		uint32_t layout_stride = alloc_args.width;
+		if (format == DRM_FORMAT_NV12)
+			layout_stride = ALIGN(layout_stride, 256);
+		drv_bo_from_format(bo, layout_stride, 1, alloc_args.height, format);
 		bo_layout_ready = true;
 		bo->meta.total_size = ALIGN(bo->meta.total_size, size_align);
 		alloc_args.drm_format = DRM_FORMAT_R8;
@@ -469,6 +475,9 @@
 	 * surface and reject the YV12 plane pitches; state that it is linear. */
 	if (format == DRM_FORMAT_YVU420_ANDROID && bo->meta.format_modifier == DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID)
 		bo->meta.format_modifier = DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR;
+	/* Lepton: spoofed NV12 is linear too; importers (VA-API) need to know. */
+	if (format == DRM_FORMAT_NV12 && bo_layout_ready)
+		bo->meta.format_modifier = DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR;
 
 	bo->priv = priv;
 	priv->drv = drv;
